\par }\pard \ltrpar\s16\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
Our sages tell us that, originally, all trees were fruit-bearing, and that this will happen when Moshiach comes .
\par A fruitless tree is a symptom of an imperfect world, for the ultimate function of a tree is to produce fruit.
\par If \'93Man is a tree of the field\'94}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn19" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [19]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  and fruit is the tree\rquote s highest achievement, there are seven fruits that crown the human and botanical harvest. 
\par These are the seven fruits and grains singled out by the Torah as exemplars of the Holy Land\rquote s fertility: wheat, barley, grapes, figs, pomegranates, olives and dates.}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn20" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [20]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par The fifteenth day of the Hebrew month of Shevat is the day designated by the Jewish calendar as the \'93New Year for Trees.\'94 On this day, we celebrate the trees of G-d\rquote s world, and the tree within us, by partaking of these seven \'93fruits,\'94
 which typify the various components and modes of human life.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \ab\af0 \ltrch \b\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
Food and Fodder}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s16\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af1\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 The Kabalistic masters tell us that each and every one of us has not one, but two souls: an \'93animal soul,\'94 which embodies our natural, self-oriented instincts; and a \'93G-dly soul\'94
 embodying our transcendent drives, our desire to escape the \'93I\'94 and relate to that which is greater than ourselves.}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn21" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [21]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par As its name implies, the animal soul constitutes that part of ourselves that
 is common to all living creatures: the instinct for self-preservation and self-perpetuation. But man is more than a sophisticated animal. There are qualities that are unique to us as human beings\emdash the qualities deriving from our \'93G-dly soul.\'94
 The point at which we graduate beyond the self and its needs (\'93How do I survive?\'94 \'93How do I obtain food, shelter, money, power, knowledge, satisfaction?\'94) to a supra-self perspective (\'93Why am I here?\'94 \'93What purpose do I serve?\'94
) is the point at which we cease to be just another animal in G-d\rquote s world and begin to realize our uniqueness as human beings.
\par This is not to say that the animal self is to be rejected in favor of the divine-human self. These are our two souls, both of which are indispensable to a life of fulfillm
ent and purpose. Even as we stimulate the divine in us to rise above the merely animal, we must also develop and refine our animal selves, learning to cultivate the constructive elements of selfhood (e.g., self-confidence, courage, perseverance) while wee
ding out the selfish and the profane.
\par \'93Wheat,\'94 a staple of the human diet,}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn22" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [22]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  represents the endeavor to nourish what is distinctly human in us, to feed the divin
e aspirations that are the essence of our humanity. Barley, a typical animal food,}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\
l "_edn23" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [23]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  represents the endeavor to nourish and develop our animal soul\emdash a task no le
ss crucial to our mission in life than the cultivation of our G-dly soul.}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn24" \\o "" }
}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [24]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \ab\af0 \ltrch \b\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
Excitement }{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s16\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af1\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 Wheat and barley, the two grains among the \'93seven fruits,\'94 represent the essentials of our inner make-up. Following these come five fruits\emdash \'93appetizers\'94 and \'93desserts\'94 on our spiritual menu
\emdash that add flavor and zest to our basic endeavor of developing our animal and G-dly souls.
\par The first of these is the grape, whose defining characteristic is joy. As the grapevine describes its product in Yotam\rquote s Parable, \'93...my wine, which makes joyous G-d and men.\'94}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn25" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [25]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par Joy is revelation. A person ignited by joy has the same basic traits he possesses in a non-joyous state\emdash 
the same knowledge and intelligence, the same loves, hates, wants and desires. But in a state of joy, everything is more pronounced: the mind keener, the loves deeper, the hates more v
ivid, the desires more aggressive. Emotions that ordinarily show only a faint intimation of their true extent now come out into the open. In the words of the Talmud, \'93When wine enters, the concealed emerges.\'94}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 
\ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn26" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [26]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par A joyless life might be complete in every way, yet it is a shallow life: everything is there, but only the barest surface is showing. Both the G-dly and the animal souls contain vast reservoirs of insight 
and feeling that never see the light of day because there is nothing to stimulate them. \'93Grape\'94 represents the element of joy in our lives\emdash the joy that unleashes these potentials and adds depth, color and intensity to everything we do.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \ab\af0 \ltrch \b\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
Involvement}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s16\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af1\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 We might be doing something fully and completely; we might even be doing it joyously. But are we there? Are we involved?
\par Involvement means more than doing something right, more than giving it our all. It means that we care, that we are invested in the task. It means that we are affected by what we are doing, for the better or for the worse.
\par The fig, the fourth of the \'93seven fruits,\'94 is also the fruit of the \'93Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil\'94\emdash the fruit of which Adam and Eve tasted, thereby committing the first sin of history.}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 
\ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn27" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [27]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  As Chassidic teaching explains, \'93knowledge\'94 (}{\rtlch \ai\af0 \ltrch \i\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 daat}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
) implies an intimate involvement with the thing known (as in the verse, \'93And Adam knew his wife\'94}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn28" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [28]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 ). Adam
\rquote s sin derived from his refusal to reconcile himself with the notion that there are certain things from which he must distance himself: he desired to intimately know every corner of G-d\rquote s world, to become involved with every one of G-d
\rquote s creations. Even evil, even that which G-d had declared out of bounds to him.}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\
l "_edn29" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [29]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par Adam\rquote s fig was one of the most destructive forces in history. In its equally powerful constructive guise, the fig represents our capacity for a deep and intimate involvement in our every positive endeavor\emdash 
an involvement which signifies that we are one with what we are doing.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \ab\af0 \ltrch \b\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 Deed }{
\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s16\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af1\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 \'93Your lips are like a thread of scarlet,\'94 sings King Solomon in Song of Songs, his celebration of the love between the Divine Groom and His bride Israel, \'93
your mouth is comely; your temple is like a piece of pomegranate within your locks.\'94}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\
l "_edn30" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [30]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
 As interpreted by the Talmud, the allegory of the pomegranate expresses the truth that, \'93Even the empty ones amongst you are full of good deeds as a pomegranate [is full of seeds].\'94}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289  HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn31" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [31]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par The pomegranate is not just a model for something that contains many particulars. It also addresses the paradox of how an individual may be \'93empty\'94 and, at the same time, be \'93full of good deeds as a pomegranate.\'94
\par The pomegranate is a highly compartmentalized fruit: each of its hundreds of seeds is wrapped in its own sac of flesh and is separated from its fellows by a tough membrane. In the same way, it is possible for a person to do good deeds\emdash 
many good deeds\emdash yet they remain isolated acts, with little or no effect on his nature and character. He may possess many virtues, but they do not become him; he may be full of good deeds, yet he remains morally and spiritually hollow.
\par If the fig represents our capacity for total involvement and identification with what we are doing, the pomegranate is its very antithesis, representing our capacity to overreach ourselves and act in a
 way that surpasses our internal spiritual state. It is our capacity to do and achieve things that are utterly incompatible with who and what we are at the present moment.
\par The pomegranate is \'93hypocrisy\'94 in its noblest form: the refusal to reconcile oneself\ltrpar  to one\rquote s spiritual and moral station as defined by the present state of one\rquote 
s character; the insistence on acting better and more G-dly than we are.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \ab\af0 \ltrch \b\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
Struggle }{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s16\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch \af1\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 For most of us, \'93life\'94 is synonymous with \'93struggle.\'94 We struggle to forge an identity under the
 heavy shadow of parental and peer influence; we struggle to find a partner in life, and then we struggle to preserve our marriage; we struggle to raise our children, and then struggle in our relationship with them as adults; we struggle to earn a living,
 and then struggle with our guilt over our good fortune; and underlying it all is the perpetual struggle between our animal and G-dly selves, between our self-oriented instincts and our aspiration to transcend the self and touch the divine.
\par The \'93olive\'94 in us is the part of ourselves that thrives on struggle, that revels in it, that would no more escape it than escape life itself. \'93Just like an olive,\'94 say our sages, \'93which yields its oil only when pressed,\'94
 so, too, do we yield what is best in us only when pressed between the millstones of life and the counter forces of a divided self.}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.meaningfullife.com/html/wir/archives/5758/Shmot/" \\l "_edn32" \\o "" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \cs15\f0\fs28\ul\cf17\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 [32]}}}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \f0\fs28\insrsid3503289\charrsid3503289 
